  "cleanup_phases": [
    "entry: rbx = the map pointer loaded from the descriptor at [rdi+0x00]; r14 = the record drop function pointer at [rdi+0x08] (a null pointer skips the scan); r12 = the record stride at [rdi+0x10]; the mask is loaded from map+0x08 and a mask of -1 skips the scan",
    "scan: control bytes are visited from index 0 upward (the byte at ctrl + index is compared against 0, and the loop advances while the subtraction does not overflow -- only the byte 0x80, the in-place fixup mark, stops the scan); the scan ends when the index arithmetic reaches the mask-derived bound",
    "per marked slot: the mask is reloaded, the slot index is wrapped (rbp & mask), 0xff is stored at ctrl + index (0x4742623) and at the mirror ctrl + (rbp & mask) + 0x10 (0x474262b), the record pointer (ctrl plus the accumulated -index*stride offset) is passed to the descriptor function pointer (call r14 at 0x4742636), and the item count at map+0x18 is decremented by one (0x474263b)",
    "finish: growth-left = cap(mask + 1) - items, with the grow packet capacity model (cmovb small-table form included), is stored at map+0x10 (0x4742663); the control pointer and the mask are never stored"
  ],
  "drop_phases": [
    "entry: the mask at map+0x08 is the gate -- zero returns at once (the static empty block is not heap); the item count at map+0x18 bounds the walk",
    "walk: control groups are loaded in order with movdqa/pmovmskb; the inverted mask selects the full (non-special) lanes; each group step moves the bucket cursor by -0x580 (16 buckets of 0x58) and an intra-group lane resolves with tzcnt and an imul by 0x58",
    "per live bucket: the key buffer at bucket+0x08 is freed through the dealloc slot when the key record first word at bucket+0x00 is nonzero (size = that word); the child S mapped array at bucket+0x28 is freed when the count at bucket+0x20 is nonzero (size = count*8); the body recurses into the child S embedded map at bucket+0x38 (self-call at 0x47429c1)",
    "finish: the body tail-jumps to the dealloc slot with base = ctrl - align16(buckets*0x58) and the total size align16(buckets*0x58) + buckets + 16; no control byte is rewritten and neither map+0x10 nor map+0x18 is stored"
  ],
  "verdicts": {
    "removal_side": "No single-entry erase body for the S-rooted map can be isolated: the censused candidate sets are empty or untied, the map operation set traced across the RE-015 packets is build / grow / lookup / replace-on-hit / whole-table drop, and the only removal-flavoured body in the cluster (0x47425c0) is the sibling grow's unwind-path cleanup of fixup-marked records -- it blanks marked slots to 0xff (slot plus mirror), drops each marked record through a descriptor function pointer, decrements items once per record and recomputes growth-left at the end. No body clears a live entry of this map to a 0x80 tombstone as a consumer erase, and no body performs backward-shift deletion for it: entries leave the S map only when the whole table is dropped by 0x4742960 or when an insert hit displaces a value into the caller's hands.",
    "grow_reachability": "The grow body 0x4742aa0 is referred to exactly once in the whole binary across every censused form: the map insert's call through slot 0x64eaf78 at 0x474ba06, passing (map, 1, map+0x20, 1). Direct E8/E9 sites: none. Other rip-relative references to the body or the slot: none. .rela.dyn addend carriers: only the slot itself; .rela.plt: none. Absolute words naming the body or the slot: only that relocation entry's own fields. Nothing reaches the grow body with a fallibility byte of 0 or an additional other than 1."
  }
}
